{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013AfERguNFX3rhaPcr7wtNs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd097-who\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/who: Show Who Is Logged On\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD who that differs from GNU who in output format, flag support, and\n6\t  header display. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n7\t  (gwho, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n8\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Show information about currently logged-in users.\n12\t  - G2: Support header display, idle time, and boot time options.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gwho via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default user listing\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must read the utmpx database and print one line per logged-in user showing login name, terminal line, login time, and remote hostname (if available), matching GNU who output format.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When given a FILE argument, must read that file as the utmpx database instead of the system default.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"who am i (or who am I) must print only the entry for the current terminal.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when the utmpx database cannot be read.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Display options\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-H or --heading must print a header line above the output.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-u or --users must show idle time for each user. Idle time is displayed as HH:MM, '.' for active (< 1 minute), or 'old' for > 24 hours.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: \"-b or --boot must show the time of the last system boot.\"\n37\t      - R2.4:\n38\t          text: \"-q or --count must print login names and a count of logged-in users, one name per column.\"\n39\t\n40\t  R3:\n41\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R3.1:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n45\t      - R3.2:\n46\t          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n47\t      - R3.3:\n48\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n49\t\n50\tnon_goals:\n51\t  - cmd/who does not implement -r (runlevel) or -d (dead processes) on macOS.\n52\t\n53\tacceptance_criteria:\n54\t  - id: AC1\n55\t    criterion: \"who prints logged-in users with terminal and time, matching gwho.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.1\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"who -H prints a header line, matching gwho -H.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.1\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"who -b prints boot time, matching gwho -b.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R2.3\n66\t  - id: AC4\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gwho passes.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R2.1\n71\t      - R2.3\n72\t  - id: AC5\n73\t    criterion: \"cmd/who compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R2.4\n83\t      - R3.1\n84\t      - R3.2\n85\t      - R3.3\n86\t\n87\tpackage_contract:\n88\t  imports:\n89\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61f0b0c3-9a9b-4443-b24b-25eb95cc8ed5","uuid":"52d455f9-6183-4938-be2f-d4dddb80f3b5","timestamp":"2026-05-27T14:28:46.163Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5583/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml","content":"id: srd097-who\ntitle: \"cmd/who: Show Who Is Logged On\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD who that differs from GNU who in output format, flag support, and\n  header display. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gwho, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Show information about currently logged-in users.\n  - G2: Support header display, idle time, and boot time options.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gwho via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default user listing\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must read the utmpx database and print one line per logged-in user showing login name, terminal line, login time, and remote hostname (if available), matching GNU who output format.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When given a FILE argument, must read that file as the utmpx database instead of the system default.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"who am i (or who am I) must print only the entry for the current terminal.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when the utmpx database cannot be read.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Display options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-H or --heading must print a header line above the output.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-u or --users must show idle time for each user. Idle time is displayed as HH:MM, '.' for active (< 1 minute), or 'old' for > 24 hours.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-b or --boot must show the time of the last system boot.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-q or --count must print login names and a count of logged-in users, one name per column.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/who does not implement -r (runlevel) or -d (dead processes) on macOS.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"who prints logged-in users with terminal and time, matching gwho.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"who -H prints a header line, matching gwho -H.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"who -b prints boot time, matching gwho -b.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gwho passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/who compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
